# Midnight indexer GraphQL endpoint behind the mobile Home screen's recent
# transactions. Pass the HTTP URL — the client derives its own WebSocket URL.
# Defaults to the preview indexer when unset.
# VITE_INDEXER_URL=https://indexer.preview.midnight.network/api/v4/graphql

# Origin of the Midnight Raffle example dApp listed in the Apps registry
# (decided 2026/08/05 — replaces the deprecated VITE_ATLAS_URL). It must be a
# separate origin from Passport for the profile consent handshake to be real.
# Defaults to http://localhost:5177 when unset. VITE_RAFFLE_NAME relabels the
# grid entry the same way VITE_LOCAL_APP_NAME relabels the local one, and
# defaults to "Midnight Raffle"; the entry itself is always listed, whether or
# not either variable is set.
# VITE_RAFFLE_URL=http://localhost:5177
# VITE_RAFFLE_NAME=Midnight Raffle

# Generic local-development slot in the Apps grid (added 2026/08/06). Point it
# at any dev server and its app appears in the grid, labelled by
# VITE_LOCAL_APP_NAME or "Local app" when that is unset. This is the variable to
# hand a third-party developer; VITE_RAFFLE_URL above is the legacy name for the
# same mechanism and keeps working. Set both and both entries appear. Unset, the
# grid is exactly as it was. Same rule as the raffle: a separate origin from
# Passport, or the consent handshake is not real.
# VITE_LOCAL_APP_URL=http://localhost:5178
# VITE_LOCAL_APP_NAME=My App

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local development origins — this app is pinned to port 5175
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The dev server binds http://localhost:5175 with `strictPort` (vite.config.ts),
# and src/main.tsx redirects any other origin to it whenever
# `import.meta.env.DEV` is set. Two consequences worth knowing before you lose
# an afternoon to them:
#
#   - if your browser lands on 5175 when you started the dev server elsewhere,
#     you did not mistype and nothing is broken — that redirect did it;
#   - a second dev server already holding 5175 collides with this one instead of
#     moving to the next free port, so start Passport first and leave 5175 to it.
#
# Nothing here overrides the pin; it is a constant in the source, deliberately,
# because Passport frames apps by URL and a handshake against a moving origin
# fails silently.

# Telegram support channel. When set, the Home screen renders a "Support on
# Telegram" pill in its footer area; when unset, no support link is shown.
# VITE_TELEGRAM_URL=https://t.me/midnightpassport

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Activation funder (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Base URL of a self-hosted passport-funder service (examples/passport-funder).
# When set, Passport asks it for two things, in order of preference:
#
#   1. SPONSORED REGISTRATION. If the funder's /status reports
#      aliasSponsorship "available", the funder registers the .night name FOR
#      the user — the user's Midnames key as owner, their account-custody
#      contract as target — paying the registry price from its own NIGHT and
#      the fees from its own DUST. The user's wallet signs nothing, spends
#      nothing, and needs to hold nothing; the funds gate is skipped entirely
#      because the user's balance is not part of the claim. The client
#      confirms the result with its OWN registry read before reporting it
#      confirmed. See src/identity/sponsoredAlias.ts.
#   2. ACTIVATION DRIP, the fallback when sponsorship is not on offer: the
#      first time a .night claim would be queued for lack of NIGHT, the funder
#      drips an activation-sized grant (default 0.001 NIGHT), the wallet
#      watches its own live balance stream for the arrival (45 s ceiling), and
#      the claim then executes immediately — sponsored fees exactly as today.
#
# A funder that refuses sponsorship for a reason self-paying can fix (out of
# NIGHT, rate ceiling, this Passport already had its one sponsored name)
# falls back to the self-paid claim, which re-runs its own funds gates and
# refuses honestly. Unset, behaviour is byte-identical to before the funder
# existed: the claim queues until the wallet is funded from the captcha
# faucet.
# VITE_FUNDER_URL=http://localhost:8799

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Choosing a network
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The whole app follows VITE_MIDNIGHT_NETWORK_ID: the wallet signs there, the
# network switcher opens there, names register there, and the faucet and
# explorer links point there. Unset means `preview`.
#
# VITE_MIDNIGHT_NETWORK_ID=preview
# VITE_MIDNIGHT_NODE_URL=https://rpc.preview.midnight.network
# VITE_MIDNIGHT_PROVING_URL=https://proof-server.preview.midnight.network
#
# Sponsored fees are ON BY DEFAULT: each public network falls back to its
# gateway (preview/preprod api-*.1am.xyz) when this is unset, because a fresh
# passkey wallet holds no DUST and cannot pay its first fee. Set the literal
# value `off` to disable sponsorship, or a URL to use a different gateway. The
# client still gates on `available > 0` from the service's own /wallet-status,
# never on a hopeful assumption.
# VITE_SPONSOR_URL=off
#
# PRE-PRODUCTION — DO NOT SET THESE YET (measured 2026/08/06)
# -----------------------------------------------------------
# Every preprod endpoint is healthy, and the sponsor is funded there — it is
# the first environment where the sponsored-fee gate genuinely opens
# (`available: 1`, ~29.8 DUST, synced). The app is fully network-generalised
# and was verified against preprod end to end: preprod addresses, preprod
# indexer, availability decoded from the preprod `.night` TLD, preprod faucet
# link, sponsor gate AVAILABLE.
#
# It still cannot ship, for one reason: the FIRST sync. A cold wallet walks the
# chain from genesis, and preprod is ~1.98M blocks deep against preview's
# ~296k. Measured in-tab, on the same machine, minutes apart:
#
#   preview   4% -> synced in ~75 s, heap steady at ~90 MB
#   preprod   3% after 150 s, heap climbing ~25 MB/s, tab CRASHES at ~4.2 GB
#
# RULED OUT 2026/08/06 — starting a NEW wallet at the chain tip.
#
# A wallet created in this app cannot have transactions older than itself, so
# it ought to be able to skip the walk. It was built and measured against the
# live preprod indexer: take the empty state the SDK serialises for a fresh
# wallet, move each component's `offset`/`appliedId` to the highest index its
# own subscription reports (`zswapLedgerEvents.maxId`, `dustLedgerEvents.maxId`,
# `UnshieldedTransactionsProgress.highestTransactionId`), and `restore()` it.
# The wallet opens and the facade reports SYNCED in ~3 s.
#
# Then the first real event arrives and the ledger throws:
#
#   values inserted non-linearly into zswap commitment tree;
#     expected to insert index 0, but received 17671.
#   values inserted non-linearly into dust commitment tree;
#     expected to insert index 0, but received 1023684.
#
# Both ZswapLocalState and DustLocalState hold a copy of a GLOBAL commitment
# tree that has to be filled from genesis in index order. The only fast-forward
# primitive in the ledger is ZswapLocalState.applyCollapsedUpdate, and the
# public indexer serves nothing that can feed it; DustLocalState has no
# equivalent at all. Splitting the difference does not help either — a
# DUST-only walk from genesis runs at ~410 events/s with the heap past 3 GB
# inside 30 s, ~1% of the stream. So skipping the walk needs state that only
# something which has already walked the chain can hand over, which is a
# service to build, not a variable to set. Until it exists, this demo stays on
# preview. The code and the full write-up are in the tip-bootstrap section of
# src/lib/walletSnapshot.ts; nothing calls it.
#
# What does now exist is a depth guard (src/lib/localWallet.ts): above 500k
# blocks a from-genesis walk is refused with an honest error instead of being
# started and killing the tab. Preview (~296k) is unaffected.
#
#   VITE_MIDNIGHT_NETWORK_ID=preprod
#   VITE_INDEXER_URL=https://indexer.preprod.midnight.network/api/v4/graphql
#   VITE_MIDNIGHT_NODE_URL=https://rpc.preprod.midnight.network
#   VITE_MIDNIGHT_PROVING_URL=https://proof-server.preprod.midnight.network
#   VITE_SPONSOR_URL=https://api-preprod.1am.xyz
